WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.790
- Our next guest has
shattered glass ceilings

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.390
and she has made history.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:08.050
And she's someone we're very
proud to call a wildflower

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.250
which is people doing incredible things

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.880
that we wanna celebrate and
highlight here on the show.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.650
When I heard her story, I freaked out.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.796
Watch this.

00:00:16.796 --> 00:00:19.379
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.750
- Hi, I'm Lauren Simmons.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.400
At 22 years old, I made history

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.720
by becoming the youngest,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.620
and the only full-time female trader

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.340
at the New York Stock Exchange.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.700
I am a Southern girl
from Marietta, Georgia.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.000
I did not have a background in finance.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.130
I've had no intention of making history.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.340
I just wanted to make my mom proud

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.340
of the first job that I got after college.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.540
I made my way to New York

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.220
and was offered a job at
the New York Stock Exchange.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.910
I just hope that my story will
inspire the next generation

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.548
to help build a great
future for themselves.

00:00:57.548 --> 00:00:58.381
(audience cheering)

00:00:58.381 --> 00:00:59.719
- Freaking me out, reading her story.

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:02.631
Please welcome someone they call

00:01:02.631 --> 00:01:06.137
the Wolfette of Wall
Street, Lauren Simmons.

00:01:06.137 --> 00:01:07.301
(audience cheering wildly)

00:01:07.301 --> 00:01:11.360
- Thank you.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.020
- I'm so excited to meet you.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.470
I did such a deep dive on your story

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:19.700
and starting out you
were studying genetics.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.440
- Yeah.
- because of your brother.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.273
- Yes.

00:01:22.273 --> 00:01:24.740
- So you were drawn to a numbers game.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:28.750
How did you find yourself in
the New York Stock Exchange?

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.560
What, what happened there?

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.760
- No linear pathway whatsoever.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.170
I went to school for genetics.

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:38.770
I was in my senior year
writing my senior thesis

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.260
and realized, hmm, this is
not something I can pursue

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.630
because I wanted to alter DNA.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:46.530
And it's illegal to
alter DNA, only in China.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.560
And since I wasn't gonna move to China

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.880
and I could not speak Mandarin,

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.900
I moved to New York, which
is the second best city.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:53.900
No, I'm kidding but,

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.060
New York is great.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.470
And you know, I went
and I really wanted to,

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.700
numbers is a universal language.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.510
And so I said, where can I
be where I can use numbers?

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:09.045
And, I ended up at New York.

00:02:09.045 --> 00:02:09.878
(audience clapping)

00:02:09.878 --> 00:02:11.656
- What I loved,

00:02:11.656 --> 00:02:14.170
and I really appreciated this too,

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:19.150
that you said somewhere,
like, be open to things

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.490
maybe you haven't studied for

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.140
or thought where your life's
trajectory was gonna go.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.460
If a job offer comes your way

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.940
that wasn't necessarily in
your wheelhouse, be open to it.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.773
Is that true?

00:02:29.773 --> 00:02:30.606
I love that.

00:02:30.606 --> 00:02:31.870
- Yeah, be open to opportunities.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.410
I think we get so fixated
on what our plan ABC is.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.290
And I think the most growth comes

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.140
from people just stepping
outside of their comfort zone,

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.050
getting a little uncomfortable
and taking a position,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.930
taking a job that you
would've never thought of.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.328
I mean, I'm sure you have, like roles--

00:02:47.328 --> 00:02:48.920
- I didn't think I'd end up here.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:52.070
I could say that, it's true.
- Which is amazing.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.980
- At one time you were the youngest,

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.091
full-time female trader on the floor.

00:02:57.091 --> 00:03:00.600
(audience cheering)

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.050
One of the stories I loved
was that when you and the boys

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.760
would go to the bar afterwards,

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.280
how would you handle that?

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.940
- I was the only woman
on a floor with 250 men.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:15.000
And, you know, as a woman
with no other women around me,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.280
you have to think of yourself.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.160
And so a lot of these meetings,
a lot of deals get closed

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.110
by going out and partying, which whatever,

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:25.810
they would pass around
rounds of tequila shots.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:29.610
And I would tell the bartender
after the first drink,

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.550
fill it up with water, put some salt,

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:33.910
add a little lime to it, make it real.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.690
And I'd just be throwing back,
you know, shots of water.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.745
- God,
(audience clapping)

00:03:38.745 --> 00:03:41.320
I wish I had done that.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.050
Cause then your, the second
half of your sentence was

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:46.500
I didn't wanna be like
the sloppy, messy girl.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.052
And I was like,

00:03:48.052 --> 00:03:50.363
(audience laughing)

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:52.170
oops!

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:55.990
I spent most of my life being
that girl, life of the party.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.573
(upbeat music)

